And I remember thinking,
"Are you out of your mind?

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:45.717 align:start size:88% position:13%
Do you know what
fascism is, or Nazism?"

00:09:45.717 --> 00:09:47.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause that was the
German spelling, you know,

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:50.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
as if we're becoming
Nazi Germany.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:54.693
- [Dave] So how do you...

00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:56.596
- Reagan explained it.

00:09:58.063 --> 00:10:02.201 align:start size:97% position:3%
We are always one generation
away from losing freedom.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:04.703
Deuteronomy explains it.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:07.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I have my series
of Bible commentaries.

00:10:07.606 --> 00:10:08.541
- Right there.

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:10.209
- Yeah, I'm very touched, yes.

00:10:10.209 --> 00:10:11.744
I am touched.

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:13.679
- Well, this is your-
- My life's project.

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:15.181
- It's your studio.

00:10:15.181 --> 00:10:16.448
- Oh, okay, so I'm less touched.

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:18.183
- You know whose name's
on the building, right?

00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:19.351 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, yeah,
that's a good point.

00:10:19.351 --> 00:10:20.586
I didn't think of that.

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:23.622
It just shows, I'm
not Mr. Prima Donna.

00:10:23.622 --> 00:10:28.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
But Deuteronomy says, "You
will talk about these things."

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.595
That is God's teachings.

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:33.298
"When you lie down,
when you rise up,

00:10:33.298 --> 00:10:36.769
when you walk by the way,
when you go to sleep."

00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:39.205
In other words, if you
don't teach your children

00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:42.174
good values all the
time, it's over.

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:45.478
And that's what happened.

00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:46.679
And I'll tell you who did it,

00:10:46.679 --> 00:10:49.048
and I knew it when I was a kid.

00:10:49.048 --> 00:10:53.686 align:start size:97% position:3%
It was the generation we
call the Greatest Generation.

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:57.590
They were the greatest
generation in many ways,

00:10:58.624 --> 00:11:00.459
but not as parents.

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:02.795
Their motto, and by the way,

00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:06.231
I said this in my 20's,
when I started lecturing.

00:11:06.231 --> 00:11:09.334 align:start size:97% position:3%
I would look at these people,
my parents' generation.

00:11:09.334 --> 00:11:13.406
I'd say, "You always say
you give our generation

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.508
everything you didn't have.

00:11:16.508 --> 00:11:21.247
The problem is you didn't give
us everything you did have."

00:11:21.247 --> 00:11:23.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
Which was love of
country, love of God,

00:11:23.482 --> 00:11:26.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
the self-control,
and all those values.

00:11:29.054 --> 00:11:32.057
- So if you saw that when you
were 20, so now we're talking,

00:11:32.057 --> 00:11:34.093
you know, 50 some odd years ago,

00:11:34.093 --> 00:11:36.495
you must really see
it when, you know,

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:38.130
so I'm a Gen X guy.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:41.200
So at 47, I'm right
now in the thick of

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.835 align:start size:84% position:16%
what is supposed to
be the group of people

00:11:42.835 --> 00:11:44.570
running the show at this point.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:45.805
And yet we're not.

00:11:45.805 --> 00:11:48.107 align:start size:88% position:13%
We have an 80 plus year
old who's president

00:11:48.107 --> 00:11:50.042 align:start size:81% position:19%
and another 80
plus year old who,

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:51.210
and I'm not an ageist of course,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:54.046
but the shift has not occurred

00:11:54.046 --> 00:11:56.716 align:start size:97% position:3%
where we have sort of younger
people running things.

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:58.551
I also think that is adding
now to some of the tension.

00:11:58.551 --> 00:11:59.785
- Oh, I wonder.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know why, exactly,
'cause I remember,

00:12:03.489 --> 00:12:05.958 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I'm not saying this
'cause I'm old now,

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:10.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I remember the
motto, one of the stupid,

00:12:10.095 --> 00:12:13.933 align:start size:97% position:3%
many stupid mottos of my
generation, the Baby Boomers,

00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:16.034
"Never trust anyone over 30."

00:12:16.034 --> 00:12:18.170
And I was 20 when
I first heard it.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.471
And I thought, "What are
you, out of your mind?"

00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:21.106
I trust Moses.

00:12:21.106 --> 00:12:22.974
He's 3,000 years old.

00:12:22.974 --> 00:12:24.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember thinking that.
- That's funny.

00:12:24.676 --> 00:12:26.812
- He's really over 30.

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:28.714
But what a stupid line is that?

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:30.950
Let's say everyone over 60

00:12:33.051 --> 00:12:35.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
was removed from all
public office in America.

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:36.955
Nothing would change.

00:12:36.955 --> 00:12:37.823
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:12:37.823 --> 00:12:38.891
- Nothing.

00:12:38.891 --> 00:12:40.092
- I think there's a slim chance

00:12:40.092 --> 00:12:41.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
we'd get some change
on the margins.

00:12:41.527 --> 00:12:42.995
Maybe just, just getting rid of

00:12:42.995 --> 00:12:44.530
some of the, like, dead wood.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:45.831
- Yeah, so you'd
have young fools.

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:47.365
- Yeah, we would just get the-

00:12:47.365 --> 00:12:48.434
- We'd just have middle aged
fools instead of old fools.

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:50.202
- Yeah.

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:52.805
Well, look, it's so
funny, 'cause you're
doing this with me.

00:12:52.805 --> 00:12:56.876 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're talking about
the ills of the world.

00:12:56.876 --> 00:12:58.477
But you always have
a smile on your face.

00:12:58.477 --> 00:13:00.045
I see you at my house, you
have a smile on your face.

00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:01.480
- Oh, you know why, okay.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:02.314
- And you've been talking
about happiness forever.

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:03.415
- That's right.

00:13:03.415 --> 00:13:04.650 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So it's an
interesting dichotomy.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.151
You're telling me, on one hand,

00:13:06.151 --> 00:13:07.319
you're worried about the
world, and I know you are.

00:13:07.319 --> 00:13:09.688 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's your life's
work to correct that.

00:13:09.688 --> 00:13:11.290 align:start size:84% position:16%
And yet you really,
if someone said to me,

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.891
"Who's the happiest
person you know?

00:13:12.891 --> 00:13:14.025
It's probably you.

00:13:14.025 --> 00:13:14.893
- Right.

00:13:14.893 --> 00:13:16.361
Well, you know-

00:13:16.361 --> 00:13:17.296
- And yet there's a whole
other series of people

00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:18.563
that think you're very scary.

00:13:18.563 --> 00:13:19.298
You're a right wing
maniac or something.

00:13:19.298 --> 00:13:20.565
- Right, yes.

00:13:20.565 --> 00:13:23.101
Like they know me, or
even know what I say.

00:13:23.101 --> 00:13:26.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
They got all their material
from another left site.

00:13:26.639 --> 00:13:27.840
- [Dave] Right.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.908 align:start size:88% position:13%
- It's very, you'll
find this very touching.

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:32.210
'cause you're very
close to Jordan.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.114 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, so Jordan
Peterson, obviously,

00:13:36.648 --> 00:13:41.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
he was at a PragerU gala
about a year and a half ago.

00:13:41.487 --> 00:13:44.155
And we had a wonderful dialogue.

00:13:44.155 --> 00:13:47.393
And I'm, of course,
a big fan of Jordan.

00:13:47.393 --> 00:13:51.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he, to his credit,
stayed afterwards

00:13:51.163 --> 00:13:53.865 align:start size:97% position:3%
to take pictures with
people and talk with people.

00:13:53.865 --> 00:13:55.901 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I was very
impressed with that,

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:57.369
'cause a lot of speakers leave.

00:13:57.369 --> 00:14:00.038
And I do what he does,
I stay, I hang around.

00:14:00.038 --> 00:14:02.207
But of course, at a Prager
event, I'm gonna hang around.

00:14:02.207 --> 00:14:03.742
Okay.

00:14:03.742 --> 00:14:07.145
Anyway, he walked over to me,
I've never told this publicly.

00:14:07.145 --> 00:14:11.283
I don't think he'd mind,
but you're so close to him.

00:14:11.283 --> 00:14:14.519
It's mind-blowing
what you just said.

00:14:14.519 --> 00:14:18.056
He said something to this
effect, I'm paraphrasing.

00:14:18.056 --> 00:14:21.360
"You know, Dennis,
I don't know anybody

00:14:22.728 --> 00:14:26.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is as intense about
the big issues as you are,

00:14:29.234 --> 00:14:33.671 align:start size:97% position:3%
and who was as happy as you
are, who was as lighthearted."

00:14:33.671 --> 00:14:37.609 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I never thought of that,
that I'm sort of unique.

00:14:37.609 --> 00:14:42.147 align:start position:0%
I don't know if I'm unique,
but sort of unique in that way.

00:14:42.147 --> 00:14:46.785
A, it's my temperament,
but B, I cultivated it.

00:14:46.785 --> 00:14:49.154
I hate being unhappy.

00:14:49.154 --> 00:14:50.022
I really hate it.

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:51.289
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:14:51.289 --> 00:14:53.993
- And I am able to
compartmentalize.

00:14:56.694 --> 00:14:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why my answer,
"Better than my country,"

00:14:59.365 --> 00:15:01.199
is such an honest answer.

00:15:01.199 --> 00:15:05.938
Am I quote-unquote depressed
about the state of America?

00:15:07.372 --> 00:15:08.306
Yes.

00:15:08.306 --> 00:15:09.374
But am I depressed?

00:15:09.374 --> 00:15:10.275
No.

00:15:10.275 --> 00:15:11.710
- Right.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:14.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of people
can't do that these days.

00:15:14.046 --> 00:15:15.146
- That's right, they can't.

00:15:15.146 --> 00:15:16.648 align:start size:88% position:13%
- They can't disconnect
those things.

00:15:16.648 --> 00:15:17.750 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, that's right, and
they can't compartmentalize.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.084
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:15:19.084 --> 00:15:21.086 align:start position:0%
- If you can't compartmentalize,
you cannot be happy.

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:25.123
Otherwise, every human being
who has had tragedy is doomed.

00:15:25.123 --> 00:15:28.427
You know how many parents I
know who have lost a child?

00:15:28.427 --> 00:15:30.796
A lot of them have been able,

00:15:30.796 --> 00:15:33.565
and it's truly to
their great credit,

00:15:33.565 --> 00:15:38.037 align:start size:97% position:3%
to walk around with an
essentially happy disposition.

00:15:39.338 --> 00:15:42.141 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's the more searing
pain a human can have,

00:15:42.141 --> 00:15:44.677
which you can only now imagine.

00:15:44.677 --> 00:15:46.478
It's the ultimate nightmare.

00:15:46.478 --> 00:15:48.280 align:start size:84% position:16%
- We had to take
Luke to the hospital.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.349
Out of nowhere, one night
something wasn't right.

00:15:50.349 --> 00:15:52.517
He was a little pale and
kind of closing his eyes.

00:15:52.517 --> 00:15:53.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
We thought something
was going on.

00:15:53.719 --> 00:15:56.288 align:start size:84% position:16%
And maybe I said
this once on camera.

00:15:56.288 --> 00:15:57.556
This is about six months ago.

00:15:57.556 --> 00:16:00.759
We were in the car,
and I spoke to God

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:04.429
to whatever extent
that I speak to God,

00:16:04.429 --> 00:16:05.931 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I said, "You could
take me right now."

00:16:05.931 --> 00:16:07.399
Like, take me instead of him.

00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:08.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, just don't
take him, yeah.

00:16:08.367 --> 00:16:09.634
- Yeah, yeah.

00:16:09.634 --> 00:16:11.803
- Oh, you know, that
gives me the chills.

00:16:11.803 --> 00:16:14.973 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I brought my first
son home from the hospital,

00:16:14.973 --> 00:16:17.409 align:start size:81% position:19%
I remember getting
out of the car,

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:21.413
crossing the street into
my house and thinking,

00:16:22.514 --> 00:16:25.818
"I have never been as
unafraid as I am now

00:16:26.718 --> 00:16:28.587
if a car were to come.

00:16:28.587 --> 00:16:31.557
All I know is this
child will be safe,

00:16:31.557 --> 00:16:32.858
and I'm okay if I'm hit."

00:16:32.858 --> 00:16:35.093
- Hmm, wow, from day one.

00:16:35.093 --> 00:16:37.162
- It's what you had just then,
you had the same exact thing.

00:16:37.162 --> 00:16:38.530
I'm just echoing what you said.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:39.465
- Yeah.

00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:42.034
- If you can't compartmentalize,

00:16:42.034 --> 00:16:44.603
you can't achieve happiness.

00:16:44.603 --> 00:16:47.139 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's too much pain
in one's own life

00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:50.508 align:start size:84% position:16%
or in the life of
the society that if,

00:16:50.508 --> 00:16:53.846 align:start position:0%
and by the way,
compartmentalize is a good term

00:16:53.846 --> 00:16:56.848
because what sank the Titanic

00:16:56.848 --> 00:16:58.850 align:start size:88% position:13%
was that the
compartments did in fact

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.452
leak one into the next.

00:17:00.452 --> 00:17:01.686
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:17:01.686 --> 00:17:02.888
- Had they not, it
would not have sunk.

00:17:02.888 --> 00:17:04.890 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Is that something
that you think,

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I actually don't wanna
do much political stuff

00:17:07.025 --> 00:17:08.793
with you today, but is
that something you think

00:17:08.793 --> 00:17:11.296
conservative-minded
people can do better

00:17:11.296 --> 00:17:13.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
than lefties,
liberals, whatever?

00:17:13.732 --> 00:17:16.068 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yes, because our whole
life isn't politics.

00:17:16.068 --> 00:17:17.703
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:17:17.703 --> 00:17:20.272
- If the country
were in good shape,

00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:22.173 align:start size:97% position:3%
I wouldn't talk about
politics five minutes a day.

00:17:22.173 --> 00:17:23.608
- Yeah.

00:17:23.608 --> 00:17:27.713 align:start position:0%
- I am forced to, 'cause I
want to help save this country.

00:17:27.713 --> 00:17:29.948
But that is their meaning.

00:17:32.651 --> 00:17:33.952
Revolution is their meaning.

00:17:33.952 --> 00:17:36.321
That's not our meaning.

00:17:36.321 --> 00:17:40.925 align:start size:97% position:3%
We get meaning from a whole
bunch of things, even hobbies.

00:17:40.925 --> 00:17:43.529 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah. It's funny 'cause when
I had you and Jordan over,

00:17:43.529 --> 00:17:45.430
and that night, it
was mostly focused on

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.431
family and whatever.

00:17:46.431 --> 00:17:48.900
But like, had we
talked politics,

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.335
it would've almost
seemed ridiculous.

00:17:50.335 --> 00:17:52.471
The word Trump did not come up.

00:17:52.471 --> 00:17:53.672
The name DeSantis
did not come up.

00:17:53.672 --> 00:17:54.873
- [Dennis] That's right.

00:17:54.873 --> 00:17:56.108 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And it would've seemed
sort of ridiculous.

00:17:56.108 --> 00:17:58.577
Why would I waste my
time with you guys

00:17:58.577 --> 00:17:59.912
talking about that stuff?

00:17:59.912 --> 00:18:01.412
Not to say it isn't important,

00:18:01.412 --> 00:18:03.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it is a
compartment, not the-

00:18:03.481 --> 00:18:04.649
- Yes.

00:18:04.649 --> 00:18:07.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it is, the further
the left you go,

00:18:09.187 --> 00:18:12.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
the more making
revolution is everything.

00:18:12.824 --> 00:18:16.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
And therefore politics
is everything.

00:18:16.528 --> 00:18:18.263
And that's a, sorry.

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:22.467
It's very embarrassing when my
own phone rumbles, you know.

00:18:22.467 --> 00:18:23.635
- Yeah this could be-

00:18:23.635 --> 00:18:25.437 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It's-
- What could be going on here?

00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:27.172
- Yeah. (laughs)
It's really a riot.

00:18:27.172 --> 00:18:28.706
You know what it's
gonna be, by the way.

00:18:28.706 --> 00:18:29.775
- Could be the Prager people,
they need you to do something.

00:18:29.775 --> 00:18:30.976
- No, no, here's the joke.

00:18:30.976 --> 00:18:32.878
You know what it'll
say on my phone?

00:18:32.878 --> 00:18:34.580
Scam Likely.

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:36.114
(Dave laughing)

00:18:36.114 --> 00:18:38.684
I get more calls from Mr.
Likely than from my wife.

00:18:38.684 --> 00:18:39.952
- They're trying to get you now.

00:18:39.952 --> 00:18:41.419
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:41.419 --> 00:18:42.821 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It could be Sue sending
you a picture of my children.

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:44.022
Anything's possible.

00:18:44.022 --> 00:18:44.823 align:start size:81% position:19%
- That is entirely
accurate, yes.

00:18:44.823 --> 00:18:46.290
- Anything's possible.

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think almost every time
I have you on camera,

00:18:48.159 --> 00:18:49.327
I repeat the same story,

00:18:49.327 --> 00:18:51.028 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I think it's
always worth repeating.

00:18:51.028 --> 00:18:52.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we can only do it
for a moment if you want.

00:18:52.798 --> 00:18:54.333
But the time that when I did

00:18:54.333 --> 00:18:55.567
the "Why I Left the Left" video

00:18:55.567 --> 00:18:57.101 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we were just getting
to know each other

00:18:57.101 --> 00:18:58.870
and it was the first time
I was on your radio show,

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:00.472
I think that afternoon,

00:19:00.472 --> 00:19:02.875
and I was dealing with a lot
of hate and all that stuff.

00:19:02.875 --> 00:19:03.842
And I said to you,
and I didn't know you

00:19:03.842 --> 00:19:05.110
the way I know you now.

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.378
And I said, "Dennis, you know,

00:19:06.378 --> 00:19:07.746
